# Capstone verification — Phandalin session 20260729

Run 2026-08-12 against CampaignGenerator PR #284 (`feat/276-genre-file-single-source`,
commit `77d6f95`). This is the #245 handoff's "Capstone verification", applied to this
session instead of ch46. Nothing in the campaign tree was modified: the render went to a
scratch directory and this report is the only file written here.

## Why this session is a valid subject

The capstone asks for "the first render ever with the full intended prompt stack (voice
specs delivered, present tense, multi-line genre block)". This session's existing
narration predates all three:

| Fact | Evidence |
|---|---|
| Existing narration rendered 2026-08-04 / 08-05 | mtimes on `narration/session_doc_scene_0*.md` |
| #247's voice-file resolver landed 2026-08-10 | `3255f9c fix(247): resolve voice-spec filenames beyond exact/first-name keys` |
| So the old render delivered **no voice spec** | Phandalin's files are `*_new_pipeline.md`, which need #247's rule (c) |
| The old render's genre was **flattened** | `narration/…_scene_02_….knobs.json` -> `narration_genre`: 7,063 chars, **0 newlines** |
| Flattened => one-line `GENRE:` label | pre-#281 `narrate.py` chose the block on `"\n" in g` |

So the before/after here isolates exactly what #276 and #247 changed. Note this is **two
variables at once** (voice specs + genre delivery), as the capstone itself specified — it is
not a single-variable experiment.

## What was run

Scenes 2 and 4, not 2 and 3. Scene 4 is Vukradin's, and capstone check 2 is specifically
about Vukradin's register. Scene 3 is Valphine's.

```bash
cd ~/src/campaigns/Phandalin
MAX_THINKING_TOKENS=0 python -m session_doc.sd_narrate \
  summaries/20260729/gm-assist.md \
  --plan summaries/20260729/narration/plan.md \
  --scene-extractions summaries/20260729/scene_extractions_smoothed \
  --per-scene-output <scratch> \
  --party docs/party.md --voice-dir voice --examples examples \
  --characters "Brewbarry, Soma, Valphine, Vukradin" \
  --narration-genre-file voice/_genre.md \
  --prose-mode --reflections --narrate-tokens 16000 \
  --scene 2 4 --model claude-fable-5 --backend claude-code
```

Knobs match the old render's recorded `.knobs.json` (tokens 16000, prose_mode, reflections,
`claude-code` subscription backend). `--reflections` was a no-op in both runs: this
campaign's `narrate.context` is empty, so there is nothing for it to inject.

`--narration-genre-file` is the new flag from #284. The campaign config was **not** migrated
for this run; the path was passed explicitly, so `~/src/campaigns` is untouched.

